Specification Tables and Strings 


Scenario Here are table options 

Given  A table to List of List of String : String   
| aa | bb |
| cc | dd |

Given  A Table to List Of List Of Object : Integer 
| 1 | 2 |
| 3 | 4 |
| 5 | 6 |

Given  A table to List of Object : ExampleClass 
| FieldA | FieldB |
| a      | b      |
| c      | d      |

Given A table to List of Object : ExampleClass Vertical 
| FieldA | a | c |
| FieldB | b | d |

Given A table to List of Object with Defaults : ExampleClass 
| FieldA |
| a      |
| c      |

Given A table to List of Object with Blanks in Values : ExampleClassWithBlanks
| Field 1 | Field 2 |
| ~       | b       |
| c       | ~       |
# Check for blanks 

Given  A table to List of Object with Blanks in Defaults : ExampleClassWithBlanks
| Field 1 |
| ~       |
| c       |
# Check for blanks 




Scenario Table without all fields uses defaults
Given A table to List of Object with Defaults : ExampleClass 
| FieldA |
| a      |
| c      |
Then table should be same as : ExampleClass
| FieldA | FieldB |
| a      | x      |
| c      | x      |

Scenario:  Transpose Table
Given A table to List of Object : ExampleClass 
| FieldA | FieldB |
| a      | b      |
| c      | d      |
Then transposed table to List of Object should be the same  : ExampleClass Vertical 
| FieldA | a | c |
| FieldB | b | d |

Attributes ExampleClass 
Description example
| Name   | Datatype | Default |
| FieldA | String   | y       |
| FieldB | String   | x       |

Attributes ExampleClassWithBlanks
Description has blanks 
| Name    | Datatype | Default |
| Field 1 | String   | ~       |
| Field 2 | String   | ~       |








